{
  "_readme": [
    "Curated, per-merchant additions to what CanadianMerchantPreIndex.swift already knows.",
    "The pre-index answers 'what is this PLACE' (MapKit gave PickMe a tidy name).",
    "A payment descriptor is a different string entirely: 'TIM HORTONS #4021 TORONTO ON',",
    "'SQ *CAFE METRO', 'UBER *EATS PENDING'. matchKeys are the normalized needles that",
    "actually appear in those descriptors; emailDomains are the sender domains an e-receipt",
    "arrives from. Both are keys the pre-index has no reason to carry and consumers of a",
    "payment feed cannot work without.",
    "",
    "matchKeys are normalized the same way merchant strings are (lowercased, diacritics",
    "folded, runs of non-alphanumerics collapsed to one space, trimmed) and matched as",
    "whole-word substrings. Omit an entry entirely when the normalized display name is",
    "already the only needle worth having — the generator derives that one for free.",
    "",
    "Add a key here ONLY when it is unambiguous on its own. 'metro' is a grocery chain AND",
    "half of 'CAFE METRO'; it earns its place because the generator matches whole words and",
    "the longest match wins, but a two-letter or generic needle ('go', 'the bay', 'shell' as",
    "a substring of 'shellfish') is how a pack starts producing confident nonsense."
  ],
